H(/^tip:clip: make a twitch clip|^🎬 clip$/i, '🎬 Clip', "Makes a Twitch clip of the last minute of your stream, like the clip button on Twitch. It only works while you're live. A pop-up gives you the link (▶ Watch it, ✂️ Trim / name it) and the link is posted in chat (Settings → 💜 Twitch → 🎬 Clips turns that off). The first time, sign in with Twitch again so Movie Royal may make clips. Key: Ctrl+Alt+C on any tab.");
H(/^tip:who can clip with !clip/i, '🙋 Who can clip with !clip', 'Tick who may type !clip in chat to clip the last minute: everyone, or only you, mods, VIPs, subs and / or followers. 🚫 None switches chat clipping off. Your own 🎬 Clip button and Ctrl+Alt+C always work. Saves right away.');
H(/^tip:show who would be allowed to clip/i, '🙋 Who can !clip?', 'Lists a pretend streamer, mod, VIP, sub, follower and new viewer, and whether each could clip with !clip with the boxes you ticked in Settings → 💜 Twitch → 🎬 Clips.', ['test']);
H(/anyone in chat can make a clip by typing/i, '🙋 !clip in chat', 'Anyone in chat can type !clip to clip the last minute. The clip is named "Clipped by" and their name, and the bot answers them with the link. At most one clip every 30 seconds. Twitch still lists you as the one who made it, because your Movie Royal makes it.');
H(/^tip:a pretend viewer types !clip/i, '💬 Pretend viewer types !clip', 'A pretend viewer types !clip, so you can see what the bot answers. Nothing is sent to Twitch.', ['test']);
H(/post the link in chat when a clip is made/i, '💬 Post the clip in chat', 'When a clip is made, the bot posts its link in your Twitch chat.');
H(/^tip:pretend to make a clip/i, '🧪 Pretend clip', 'Shows what you see when a clip works. Nothing is sent to Twitch and no clip is made.', ['test']);
// 🥚 The egg game (1.100.0): every control on the Eggs tab carries its own tip (shown as 💡 in help mode) + the Help tab section
H(/^tip:the egg game: viewers hatch eggs into creatures/i, '🥚 Eggs', 'The egg game: every viewer has an egg that fills while they watch and chat (faster with subs, gifts, bits and tips). It hatches into one of 120 original creatures, which level up, evolve and battle in chat. One profile across Twitch and Kick.');
H(/^(?:🟢 Make it on Kick|🟢 Pretend Kick redeem)/i, '🟢 Kick channel points', 'Kick has channel points too. 🟢 Make it on Kick puts the Buy an egg reward on your Kick channel (or finds the one already there); after that the app reads who redeemed it every few seconds and gives them an egg. It never accepts, rejects or refunds a redemption. 🟢 Pretend Kick redeem tries it with a pretend Kick viewer; nothing is sent to Kick.');
H(/^(?:💿 Pretend RateYourMusic file|#sgImpWho\b|One rating column is)/i, '💿 RateYourMusic import', 'Bring your album ratings over from RateYourMusic. On rateyourmusic.com open your own profile, scroll to the bottom and press Export your data, then pick that file on the Songs tab → Import. Every album and single you rated comes in with its rating. "One rating column is" says whose ratings they are. When a song by one of those artists plays, the album ratings show on the Now playing card. The app only reads the file; it never visits RateYourMusic. The test button reads a small pretend file and adds nothing.');
H(/^(?:🛒 Pretend buys an egg)/i, '🥚 Egg game tests', 'A pretend viewer redeems the Buy an egg reward. If their incubator is empty the egg starts incubating; otherwise it waits in their nest. The bot\'s line shows in the test chat. No channel points are used.', ['test']);
H(/^(?:✨ Make the reward|Price \(channel points\)|🥚 Give an egg)/i, '🛒 Getting eggs', 'Everyone gets 1 free egg. More eggs are bought with channel points (the Buy an egg reward): a viewer can own many, but only one incubates at a time and the next starts by itself when one hatches. Price = what one egg costs. ✨ Make the reward puts the reward on Twitch if it is missing. 🥚 Give an egg adds eggs to someone by hand (handy for Kick viewers, who have no channel points).');
H(/^(?:🏟️ Chat battle with creatures|💪 Pretend skills \+ powers)/i, '🥚 Egg game tests', 'Try the creature side of the Chat battle. 🏟️ runs a practice Chat battle where every piece is a creature with its level on it, and tells you at the end how much XP they would have earned. 💪 levels a pretend viewer\'s creature up, then they look at its skills and powers and put a power on through the pretend chat. Nothing real is changed.', ['test']);
H(/^(?:Creatures fight in the Chat battle|Stronger creature = better odds|XP for fighting|XP for winning|✨ Skills \(they learn one per form\)|💪 Powers \(viewers put them on\))/i, '⚔️ Chat battles, skills and powers', 'When someone joins your Chat battle, the creature they have out is their piece, and every creature that fights earns XP (the winner\'s the most). A stronger creature can get slightly better odds. Skills: one per form, they go off by themselves in !battle fights. Powers: unlock by level, viewers put them on with !power; a creature wears 1, 2 or 3 depending on its form.');
H(/^(?:📋 Check the egg game|🥚 Add pretend players|🐣 Hatch a pretend egg|⚔️ Pretend battle|💬 Pretend viewer types !egg|🧹 Remove the pretend players|👀 Viewer page \(pretend\)|👀 Creature chat box \(pretend\))/i, '🥚 Egg game tests', 'Tries the egg game with pretend viewers. Nothing is sent to Twitch or Kick, and the pretend players can be removed again.');
H(/^(?:🔄 Send it now|tip:send the page and the newest eggs)/i, '🌐 Viewer website', "Sends the egg page and the newest eggs and creatures to your own 24/7 bot's website right now. It also happens by itself every few minutes when something changed. Only names, eggs and creatures are sent: what chat already sees.", ['eggs']);
H(/^tip:show the test tab's tests and checklist/i, '🧪 Show the Test tab', "Shows the Test tab's tests and checklist, for trying things without going on stream. Off = that tab only shows ⚠️ Errors (what went wrong, in plain words).");
H(/^(?:🚚 What moves over|from (?:Public|Derek's|Kirb's|True's|Birx)|tip:(?:show what moves over when this edition is installed|pick the edition someone had before installing this one))/i, '🚚 Moving between editions', "Installing a different edition over the one you have keeps everything: lists, wheels, history, people and settings. This shows the few things that get changed to fit the new edition (pretend: nothing is changed).", ['test']);
H(/^(?:🎵 Song requests|🍿 Movie night|tip:chat bot: show (?:song requests|movie night))/i, '🤖 Parts of the chat bot', "Song requests and Movie night live inside the Chat bot tab: these buttons open them.", ['bot']);
H(/^(?:🎼 Music only|🛡️ DMCA-free music only|📃 Stream-safe channels|↺ Built-in list|tip:(?:only youtube videos in the music category|only music from stream-safe channels|the channels that count as dmca-free|one youtube channel name per line|put the built-in list back))/i, '🎼 What can be requested', "Music only takes just YouTube videos in the Music category. DMCA-free music only takes just music from the stream-safe channels on the list (chat has to send a link or a name the bot can find there). No list can promise a song is safe.");
H(/^(?:🔎 Look typed song names up on YouTube|🔎 YouTube readers|tip:(?:when chat types a song's name instead of a link|checks, on small sample pages, that the app can read a youtube))/i, '🔎 Song names', "Chat can type a song's name instead of a link: the bot looks it up on YouTube and adds the first result that fits your rules.");
H(/^tip:where you are in the song: drag to fast forward or rewind/i, '⏩ Where the song is', "Shows where you are in the song and how long it is. Drag it to fast forward or rewind. It works while the song plays here.", ['chat']);
// 💬 Chat dashboard (1.99.0; Birx's layout 1.106.0)
H(/^(?:Now|History|tip:(?:the song that is up now, with play|the songs that were played before, newest first))/i, '🎵 Now / History', "Now shows the song that's up, with play, skip and the stars. History lists the songs that were played, newest first, so you can go back and rate them.", ['chat']);
H(/^(?:💿 RYM|tip:look this song up on rateyourmusic)/i, '💿 RateYourMusic', "Opens RateYourMusic's search for this song in your browser, so you can rate it on your own account there. The app never visits or changes RateYourMusic itself.", ['chat']);
H(/^(?:▶ Play|⏸ Pause|⏭ Skip|tip:(?:play this song here|pause the song|skip to the next song in the queue|how loud the song plays here))/i, '🎵 Play, skip, volume', "Plays the song that's up right here in the app (it needs a YouTube link), pauses it, or skips to the next one in the queue. The slider is how loud it plays; it's remembered.", ['chat']);
H(/^tip:.*rating: [\d.]+ of 5 stars/i, '⭐ Stars', "Five stars for each of you. Click the left half of a star for a half star; click the same star again to clear it. Ratings are kept in the song database and show again when the song comes back.", ['chat']);
H(/^(?:⏳ \d+ min|tip:start the last call countdown)/i, '⏳ Last call', "Starts the last call: chat is told, a clock shows on stream, and voting closes by itself when it reaches 0. People can still vote or change their vote until then.", ['chat']);
H(/^(?:✅ Right|❌ Wrong|Skip|tip:(?:the guess for this vote was|no guess was made for this vote|more votes are waiting behind this one))/i, '🗳️ Vote pop-up', "One pop-up per vote or vote change, in the order chat voted. It shows who voted, how long they've followed, the movie, and what else they typed. Click Right or Wrong for the guess (or Skip) and the next vote shows.");
H(/^(?:↩ Back to mine|tip:(?:back to your own edition|switch to another edition's look))/i, '👀 Seeing another edition', "Your app is showing what another edition gets (its name, tabs and extras, no dev things). Pick another edition here, or ↩ Back to mine to get everything back. Nothing is saved or removed.");
H(/^(?:preview|tip:show a small muted preview of your own stream)/i, '📺 Your stream', "A small, muted preview of your own stream next to chat, so you can see what viewers see. It runs a few seconds behind (Twitch's delay). Untick Preview to save your PC some work.", ['chat']);
// 🎵 Song requests + ratings (1.98.0): every control on the Songs tab carries its own tip (shown as 💡 in help mode) + the Help tab section
H(/^tip:song requests: the queue, what's playing/i, '🎵 Songs', "Song requests: chat asks with !sr, you see the queue, rate each song (two ratings), and everything is kept in a searchable song database. Old song lists, ratings and banned songs can be imported.");
H(/^(?:⏭ Next song|tip:move on: the next song in the queue)/i, '⏭ Next song', "Moves on: the next song in the queue becomes Now playing. The one that was playing goes into the song database with its ratings.", ['songs']);
H(/^tip:.*rating for this song \(out of/i, '⭐ Rating', "Each song has two ratings. They're kept in the song database; when the song is played again the old ratings show and can be changed.", ['songs', 'test']);
H(/^(?:👀 Show what's in it|📥 Import \d|tip:(?:read the file or the pasted text|add what was found to your|pick the file with your old songs|paste a list: one song|what you are importing|when a song already has a rating here))/i, '📥 Import songs', "Bring over an old song list, old ratings or banned songs: a spreadsheet (Excel / CSV) whose first line names the columns, a text file, or pasted lines (one song or YouTube link per line). You see what was found first; nothing you already have is lost.", ['songs']);
H(/^(?:📋 Check the song rules|🎵 Fill a pretend queue|🙋 Pretend viewer asks for a song|🧹 Remove the pretend songs)/i, '🎵 Song tests', 'Tries song requests with pretend songs and viewers. Nothing is sent to Twitch and nothing is looked up.');
// 🔊 Sound alerts tab + 🧳 bring everything over (1.101.0)
H(/^(?:➕ New sound alert|tip:chat bot: (?:make a new sound alert|change this sound alert|save this sound alert|the sound alert's command|pick the sound file|who may use this sound alert|a line the bot says in chat when the sound plays))/i, '🔊 Sound alert', "A command that plays a sound, like !airhorn. Type the command, pick a sound file, set how loud it is, who can use it and how long before it can be used again. It can also say a line in chat.", ['bot']);
H(/^tip:chat bot: (?:play this sound alert now|turn this sound alert on or off|delete this sound alert|find a sound alert)/i, '🔊 Sound alerts', '▶ plays the sound so you can hear it, ✅ / ▶ Off switches it on or off, ✏️ changes it, 🗑 deletes it.', ['bot']);
H(/^tip:chat bot: the address of the sound alert page/i, '📺 Sound alerts on stream', 'Add this address to OBS as a Browser source. It shows nothing; the sound alerts play through it, so they go out on stream at the volume you set in OBS.', ['bot']);
H(/^(?:#baFiles\b|#baRep\b|✅ Bring it all over|tip:chat bot: (?:pick the files streamlabs chatbot made|add everything that was found))/i, '🧳 Bring everything over', 'Moves what you built in Streamlabs Chatbot here in one go. In Streamlabs Chatbot: Connections → Cloud → Pick Folder → Save Settings → Create Excel Files. Pick the files it made (several at once). You see what was found first; then ✅ Bring it all over adds the commands, sound alerts, timers and quotes.', ['bot']);
H(/^(?:🔊 Pretend viewer uses a sound alert|🧳 Check the bring-everything-over import|tip:(?:makes a !testbeep sound alert|reads a pretend streamlabs chatbot export))/i, '🤖 Chat bot tests', 'Tries a sound alert with a pretend viewer (you hear a short beep), or checks that a pretend Streamlabs Chatbot export is read right. Nothing is sent to your real chat.');
// 🔊 Sound alerts (1.98.0)
H(/^(?:#bcSnd\b|#bcVol\b|▶ Play|✕ No sound|tip:chat bot: (?:pick a sound file|how loud this command|play this command's sound|take the sound off))/i, '🔊 Sound alert', "A command can play a sound when it's used (like !airhorn). Pick a sound file and a volume; ▶ Play lets you hear it. You can leave the answer empty. On stream it plays through the soundboard page in OBS (or the battle screen in OBS), otherwise in the app.", ['bot']);
// 🎂 Birthdays (1.96.0)
H(/^(?:🎂 Birthdays on|tip:turn birthdays on or off)/i, '🎂 Birthdays', 'Viewers save their birthday in chat with !bday and a date (month and day only: a year is never asked for or kept). The first time they chat on their birthday, the bot wishes them a happy birthday. Everything stays on this PC.');
H(/^(?:#bdCmd\b|tip:what chat types to save their birthday)/i, 'Birthday command', 'What viewers type, followed by the date: !bday 3/14 or !bday March 14. The command alone tells them what is saved.');
H(/^(?:#bdDays\b|tip:how many days a viewer has to wait before changing their birthday)/i, 'Change it every … days', 'After saving a birthday in chat, a viewer has to wait this long before changing it again (30 days). You can always change or remove one by hand here.');
H(/^(?:Wish them a happy birthday|tip:wish someone a happy birthday|tip:what the bot says\. \{name\})/i, 'Happy birthday wish', 'The first time someone chats on their birthday, the bot says this in chat (once that day). {name} becomes their name.');
H(/^(?:#bdName\b|#bdDay\b|🎂 Save a birthday|tip:save this person's birthday by hand|tip:the chat name of the person whose birthday|tip:their birthday: just the month and day)/i, '🎂 Save a birthday', "Add or change someone's birthday yourself: type their chat name and the month and day (3/14 or March 14, no year). No waiting time applies to you.");
H(/^(?:🎂 Saved birthdays|tip:everyone whose birthday is saved|tip:remove .*'s birthday)/i, '🎂 Saved birthdays', 'Everyone whose birthday is saved, by date. ✕ removes one.');
H(/^(?:📋 Check the birthday rules|tip:walks the birthday rules through)/i, '📋 Check the birthday rules', 'Shows that saving, the 30-day wait, the once-a-day wish and "a year is never kept" all work, with a pretend viewer. Nothing is saved.');
H(/^(?:🎂 Pretend viewer saves a birthday|🎉 Pretend birthday person chats|🧹 Remove the pretend birthday|tip:a pretend viewer (saves today|whose birthday is today)|tip:removes the pretend viewer's birthday)/i, '🎂 Pretend birthday', 'Tries birthdays with a pretend viewer through the pretend chat. Nothing is sent to Twitch.');
// 🔐 Safety & privacy (1.96.0)
H(/^(?:🛡️ Run the safety check|tip:runs the safety checks now)/i, '🛡️ Safety check', "Checks, right now, that only this PC can reach the app, that pages on other websites are turned away, and that the lock's codes work the way authenticator apps expect. Nothing is changed.");
H(/^(?:📄 What is sent where|tip:a plain list of everything the app sends)/i, '📄 What is sent where', 'A plain list: what stays on your PC, what the app never asks for, and which services it talks to (only the ones you connected). Nothing is sent to the makers of the app.');
H(/^(?:🔐 Set up the lock|tip:set up the lock: scan a picture)/i, '🔐 Set up the lock', "Optional 2-step lock. Scan a picture with an authenticator app on your phone, type the code it shows, and from then on the control panel asks for a 6-digit code before it opens. You get 8 backup codes in case you lose your phone. Stream screens, OBS and the Stream Deck keep working while it's locked.");
H(/^(?:ask for the code:|tip:how often this pc is asked for the code)/i, 'Ask for the code', 'How often this PC is asked: every time the app opens (safest), once a day, or once every 30 days.');
H(/^(?:🔒 Lock now|tip:lock the control panel right now)/i, '🔒 Lock now', 'Locks the control panel right away. It asks for the code from your phone again.');
H(/^(?:🔑 New backup codes|tip:make 8 fresh backup codes)/i, '🔑 New backup codes', 'Makes 8 fresh backup codes and cancels the old ones. A backup code opens the lock once if you lose your phone. You need a code from your phone to do this.');
H(/^(?:Turn the lock off|tip:switch the lock off)/i, 'Turn the lock off', 'Switches the lock off, so the control panel opens without a code. You need a code from your phone to do this.');
H(/^(?:✅ Turn the lock on|tip:check the code and switch the lock on|tip:the 6-digit code your authenticator app shows)/i, 'Turn the lock on', 'Type the 6 digits your authenticator app shows right now. If they match, the lock is on and your backup codes are shown.');
H(/^(?:I saved them|📋 Copy|tip:copy the backup codes|tip:close this window \(the codes)/i, 'Backup codes', 'Save these somewhere safe. If you lose your phone, one backup code opens the lock (each works once). They are only shown this one time.', ['settings']);
H(/^(?:🔐 Open the lock settings|tip:open settings → account & updates, where the lock)/i, '🔐 Lock settings', 'Opens Settings → 👤 Account & updates, where the lock is set up, changed or turned off.');
// 🧰 Chat tab tools + raid wait (1.109.0)
H(/^(?:🧰 Stream tools)/i, '🧰 Stream tools', 'The box under the alerts on the Chat tab: a 🎬 Clip button and your own buttons that switch OBS to a scene.');
H(/^(?:⚙ Pick scenes|tip:pick which of your obs scenes)/i, '⚙ Pick scenes', 'Tick the OBS scenes you want as buttons on the Chat tab. OBS has to be open so the app can read your scenes.');
H(/^tip:(?:switch obs to the scene|give this obs scene a button)/i, '🎞️ Scene button', 'Click to switch OBS to that scene right away.');
H(/^(?:🎞️ Pretend scene switch|🎵 Check !mysongs|💬 Open the Chat tab|tip:pretends to press a scene button|tip:walks the song rules through with pretend people, including)/i, '🧪 Chat tab tools test', 'Pretend checks for the Chat tab’s scene buttons and the !mysongs command. OBS isn’t touched and nothing is typed in chat.');
H(/^(?:#rdDelay\b|tip:how long to wait before the raid)/i, '⏱️ Raid wait', 'How long the app waits after you press 🚀 Raid before the raid starts. Chat is told, and you can cancel while it counts down. All the way left = right away.');
// 🚀 Raid tab (1.95.0)
H(/^tip:(?:who you follow that's live right now)/i, '🚀 Raid', 'The Raid tab: every channel you follow that is live right now, the ones you raided most recently first. Click one to preview it, then 🚀 Raid sends your viewers there.');
H(/^(?:🚀 Raid\b|tip:raid .* now: your viewers)/i, '🚀 Raid', "Starts a raid to that channel. Twitch counts down about 90 seconds (or press Raid Now in your Twitch chat), then your viewers are sent over. You're asked to confirm first, and you can cancel during the countdown.", ['raid']);
H(/^tip:show .* in the preview/i, '👀 Preview', 'Click a channel to see its live picture on the right before you raid it.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:🔄 Refresh|tip:ask twitch again who is live)/i, '🔄 Refresh', 'Asks Twitch again who is live right now. It also refreshes by itself every minute while this tab is open.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:sort:|tip:the order of the live channels)/i, 'Sort', "The order of the list: the channels you raided most recently first (the usual), the ones you haven't raided for the longest, or by how many people are watching. Your choice is remembered.", ['raid']);
H(/^(?:✖ Cancel the raid|tip:stop the raid before it goes)/i, '✖ Cancel the raid', 'Stops a raid during the Twitch countdown, before your viewers are sent.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:🔇 Preview sound|🔊 Preview sound|tip:turn the preview's sound)/i, 'Preview sound', "The preview starts muted so your stream doesn't hear the other channel. Click to hear it, click again to mute.", ['raid']);
H(/^(?:↗ Open on Twitch|tip:open their channel on twitch)/i, '↗ Open on Twitch', 'Opens that channel on Twitch in your browser.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:🕘 Who you raided|tip:the channels you raided, newest first)/i, '🕘 Who you raided', "The channels you raided, newest first. It's kept on this PC only and is what the sorting uses. Raids you start by typing /raid in chat are counted too.", ['raid']);
H(/^(?:✕ Forget|tip:forget that you raided)/i, '✕ Forget', 'Forgets that you raided that channel. It only changes the sorting on this tab.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:🔑 Sign in with Twitch again|tip:sign in with twitch again so the raid tab)/i, '🔑 Sign in with Twitch again', 'Twitch asks you once to let the app see which channels you follow. That list is only used to show who is live on this tab.', ['raid']);
H(/^(?:🧪 Show me with pretend channels|🚀 Open with pretend channels|tip:fills the raid tab with 5 pretend)/i, '🧪 Pretend channels', 'Fills the Raid tab with 5 pretend live channels so you can try it. Raiding one is pretend: nothing is sent to Twitch.');
H(/^(?:📋 Check the sorting|tip:walks the sorting through)/i, '📋 Check the sorting', 'Shows the order each way of sorting gives, with pretend channels. Nothing is saved.');
H(/^(?:🧹 Remove the pretend channels|tip:takes the pretend channels away)/i, '🧹 Remove the pretend channels', 'Takes the pretend channels away: the Raid tab shows the real channels you follow again.');
// 🍿 Movie night voting (1.93.0)
H(/^(?:a new day starts at|tip:the hour in the morning when a new day starts)/i, 'A new day starts at', 'Late-night streams: going live after midnight but before this hour still counts as the day before (live at 1:30 AM Tuesday counts as Monday). It decides whether a birthday lands on a Wednesday or Sunday.');
H(/^tip:(?:filter everything on this tab)/i, '🔍 Search', "Type to filter this tab: tonight's movies, who asked, the voters and the per-chatter stats.");
H(/^tip:(?:start the last call countdown)/i, '⏳ Last call', 'Starts the countdown at the end of voting (5 minutes unless you change the box next to it). Chat is told, a clock shows in the on-stream vote box, a one-minute warning is posted, and voting closes by itself at 0. People can vote or change their vote until then.');
H(/^tip:(?:how many minutes the last call)/i, '⏳ Last call minutes', 'How long the last call countdown runs. Saved for next time.');
H(/^tip:(?:stop the countdown: voting stays open)/i, '✋ Stop the countdown', 'Stops the last call countdown. Voting stays open until you close it or start the countdown again.');
H(/^tip:(?:close voting now)/i, '⏹ Close voting', 'Closes voting right away. The bot tells chat the winner (or the tie) and the on-stream box shows it.');
H(/^tip:(?:post and pin the list of movies)/i, '📌 Pin again', "Posts the list of tonight's movies in chat again and pins it, for people who came late.");
H(/^tip:(?:open voting: the list of movies)/i, '▶ Open voting', "Opens voting: the numbered list of tonight's movies is posted and pinned in chat, and chat can vote with !vote and a number or a name.");
H(/^tip:(?:start a fresh night)/i, '🆕 New night', "Starts a fresh night. Tonight's votes and result are saved under Past nights, then everyone's votes, the raiders and the first-in-chat are wiped. Your movie list stays unless you type CLEAR.");
H(/^tip:(?:the guess for this vote was right|change this vote's guess to right)/i, '✅ Right', "Click when the guess for this person's vote was right. It counts on the on-stream guess counter and in the stats for tonight, all time and that chatter.");
H(/^tip:(?:the guess for this vote was wrong|change this vote's guess to wrong)/i, '❌ Wrong', "Click when the guess for this person's vote was wrong. It counts in the stats for tonight, all time and that chatter.");
H(/^tip:(?:no guess was made for this vote)/i, 'Skip', 'Leaves this vote out of the guess count (nobody guessed it).');
H(/^tip:(?:open the movie night tab)/i, '🍿 Movie night', 'Opens the 🍿 Movie night tab.');
H(/^tip:(?:a movie to add to tonight)/i, 'Movie name', "Type a movie for tonight's list, then press ➕ Add (or Enter).");
H(/^tip:(?:who asked for the movie you're adding|who asked for this movie)/i, 'Asked by', 'Who asked for this movie. It can be left empty.');
H(/^tip:(?:add this movie to tonight)/i, '➕ Add', "Adds the movie to tonight's list. You can still add movies while voting is open (they go at the end, so the numbers chat sees don't change).");
H(/^tip:(?:paste a whole list at once)/i, '📋 Paste a list', "Paste all of tonight's movies in one go: one per line, with who asked after a | if you like (Jaws | bob). It replaces the list, so use it before voting opens.");
H(/^tip:(?:the movie's name \(chat can vote)/i, 'Movie', "The movie's name. Chat can vote by its number or by typing its name (or the start of it).");
H(/^tip:(?:move this movie up the list|move this movie down the list)/i, '▲ ▼ Move', 'Moves the movie up or down. The numbers chat votes with follow the order, so this only works while voting is closed.');
H(/^tip:(?:take this movie off tonight)/i, '✕ Remove', "Takes the movie off tonight's list (only while voting is closed, because the numbers would change).");
H(/^tip:(?:who you're adding a vote for)/i, 'Chat name', "The chat name of the person whose vote you're adding by hand.");
H(/^tip:(?:the movie this person votes for)/i, 'Movie', 'The number or name of the movie they vote for.');
H(/^tip:(?:count this vote by hand)/i, '➕ Add a vote', 'Counts a vote for someone by hand (a vote said out loud, say). The same rules apply: their votes and their change are used up the same way.');
H(/^tip:(?:clear the first one in chat)/i, '🥇 First in chat', 'The first person to type in chat tonight gets two votes. ✕ clears it, and the next person to type becomes the first.');
H(/^tip:(?:take this raider off|take this one off)/i, '✕ Take off', 'Removes this person from the list (they go back to the normal one vote unless another reason gives them two).');
H(/^tip:(?:the chat name for the birthday, raider)/i, 'Chat name', "The chat name of the person you're giving a birthday, a raid or an extra vote.");
H(/^tip:(?:their birthday \(month\/day\))/i, 'Birthday', 'Their birthday as month/day, like 3/14 or March 14. Only needed for 🎂 Save birthday.');
H(/^tip:(?:save this person's birthday)/i, '🎂 Save birthday', 'Saves their birthday. When it lands on a Wednesday or a Sunday they get two votes that night. Birthdays are kept from night to night.');
H(/^tip:(?:mark this person as a raider tonight)/i, '🚀 Raided', "Gives this person the raider's two votes tonight. Raids that Twitch tells the app about are added by themselves; this is for one it missed.");
H(/^tip:(?:give this person one more vote tonight)/i, '➕ Extra vote', 'Gives this person one more vote tonight, on top of the rules.');
H(/^tip:(?:show the vote box on stream)/i, '📺 Vote count on stream', 'Shows the vote box (each movie with its votes, the last call clock and the guess counter) in the OBS browser source below. Untick to hide it without touching OBS.');
H(/^tip:(?:the bot answers each vote in chat)/i, '💬 Answer each vote', 'The bot answers each vote in chat ("voted for #3…") so people know it counted. Untick on busy nights to keep chat calmer.');
H(/^tip:(?:what chat types to vote)/i, 'Command', 'What chat types to vote. !vote unless you change it.');
H(/^tip:(?:how many times each person can change)/i, 'Changes each', 'How many times each person may change a vote. The rule is 1.');
H(/^tip:(?:the address of the on-stream vote box)/i, 'Vote box address', 'Add this address to OBS as a Browser source (1920 × 1080) to show the votes on stream. Add ?side=left or ?at=bottom to move the box.');
H(/^tip:(?:copy the vote box's address)/i, '📋 Copy', "Copies the vote box's address so you can paste it into an OBS Browser source.");
H(/^tip:(?:see what the vote box looks like|see what the on-stream vote box)/i, '👀 The vote box', 'Opens the on-stream vote box in a small window with pretend votes, the last call clock and the guess counter.');
H(/^tip:(?:tonight's movies, chat's votes and the guess counter)/i, '🍿 Movie night', "Movie night voting: type tonight's movies, open voting (the list is pinned in chat), chat votes with !vote, every vote pops up so you can click if the guess was right, and the count shows on stream.");
H(/^tip:(?:walks the voting rules through)/i, '📋 Check the voting rules', 'Runs the voting rules with pretend people on a pretend night and shows what each was allowed to do: 1 vote + 1 change, 2 votes for a raider, the first one in chat and a Wednesday / Sunday birthday. Nothing is saved.');
H(/^tip:(?:adds 4 pretend movies)/i, '📋 Fill a pretend list', 'Adds four pretend movies so you can try voting. Only works while your list is empty.');
H(/^tip:(?:a pretend viewer votes for a random movie)/i, '🗳️ Pretend viewer votes', 'A pretend viewer types the vote command for a random movie in the pretend chat. Voting is opened quietly first if it was closed. Nothing is sent to Twitch.');
H(/^tip:(?:a pretend raid: pretend_raider)/i, '🚀 Pretend raid', 'Pretends pretend_raider raided, so they get two votes tonight.');
H(/^tip:(?:takes the pretend voters and their votes)/i, '🧹 Clear the pretend voters', 'Removes the pretend people and their votes, so the night is clean again.');
H(/^tip:also offer test builds/i, '🧪 Test builds', 'Normally Movie Royal only offers the latest release. Tick this to also be offered test builds (pre-releases): newer, but less tried. Leave it off unless you are helping test.');
H(/^tip:(look like another edition|switch the app to another edition|switch to another edition)/i, '👀 See another edition', 'Makes your app look like the Public, Kirb, True or Birx edition: the parts that edition leaves out are hidden, so you can try it before giving it to them. Nothing is removed. Pick Mine (or restart) to get everything back.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:show which edition of movie royal/i, '🎭 Which edition is this?', 'Shows which edition of Movie Royal this copy is (the one for everyone, or one made for a streamer), its version and which GitHub it gets updates from.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:open settings → account & updates, where the edition/i, '👤 Account & updates', 'Opens Settings → 👤 Account & updates, where the edition and the update settings are.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:🎙️ prize description/i, '🎙️ Prize description', 'A short game-show style paragraph about this thing. It shows on the 🏆 Last winner card of the Marathon tab when it wins, so you can read it out. Click to write or change it; empty = none.');
H(/^tip:list every thing in the marathon battle with its prize/i, '🎙️ Prize descriptions', 'Lists every thing in your marathon battle with its prize description, so you can check none is missing.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:pretend to make a clip while kick|pretend kick clip/i, '🟢 Pretend Kick clip', 'Shows what you see when you clip while Kick is your platform: OBS saves the last minute as a video file. Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:open the folder this clip was saved in/i, '📂 Open the folder', 'Opens the folder on your PC where OBS saved this clip.');
H(/^tip:pretend the clip fails/i, "🧪 Pretend I'm not live", 'Shows the message you get when Twitch cannot make a clip because the stream is not live.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:open settings → twitch, where your latest clips/i, '📋 My clips', 'Opens Settings → 💜 Twitch → 🎬 Clips: your latest clips with links to watch or trim them.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:game capture: which capture card/i, '📺 Capture card', 'Pick the capture card whose picture you want to see (your Elgato). It can only be shown by one program at a time: close the Elgato app, and switch off its source in OBS if that shows the card itself.');
H(/^tip:game capture: where the game's sound/i, '🔊 Game sound', "Where the game's sound comes from: usually the same capture card. Pick 🔇 No sound if you already hear the game another way.");
H(/^tip:game capture: the picture size/i, '🖼️ Picture', 'The picture size and speed Movie Royal asks the capture card for. If the card cannot do it, it gives the closest it can; the line under the buttons says what you got.');
H(/^tip:game capture: how loud/i, '🔈 Volume', "How loud the game's sound is inside Movie Royal.");
H(/^tip:game capture: start or stop/i, '▶ Start / ⏹ Stop', 'Starts or stops showing the capture card. It keeps playing when you look at another tab, and starts by itself next time you open this tab. Key: S.');
H(/^tip:game capture: fill the whole screen/i, '⛶ Fullscreen', 'Fills the whole screen with the game. Esc, F or a double-click leaves it. The mouse pointer hides after a moment.');
H(/^tip:game capture: look again/i, '🔄 Find my capture card', 'Looks again for capture cards and sound inputs, for when you plugged one in after opening Movie Royal.');
H(/^tip:game capture: how see-through the fps/i, '👻 FPS see-through', 'How see-through the FPS number in the corner is, so it covers less of the game: 0% is solid, 90% is barely there. It starts at 50%.');
H(/^tip:game capture: show the game's fps/i, '📈 Show FPS', "Shows a number in the upper right corner of the picture. The big number is the game's own speed: how many different pictures a second. The small one is what the capture card sends (usually 60). A still picture, like a menu, reads low.");
H(/^tip:open the game capture tab with a pretend game/i, '🧪 Pretend game', 'Opens the 🎮 Game capture tab with a pretend game picture (no capture card needed) so you can check the FPS number: it should read about the number on the button.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:check whether the battle sound inside movie royal is quiet/i, '🔇 Is the battle quiet?', 'Says whether the battle inside Movie Royal is making sound right now. While the 🎮 Game capture tab is open it is quiet; your stream still hears the battle from OBS.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:play the jump scare on top of whatever you're using/i, '😱 Pop the scare up on my screen too', 'When a follow, sub, gift sub, bits, tip or raid comes in, the same Neon Nights jump scare as your StreamElements alerts pops up in a see-through window on top of whatever you are using, on every screen (clicks go through it and it never takes your keyboard), so it scares YOU even when you are in a game. Small / medium / big go by the money, like the alerts. Works over games in windowed or borderless mode; a game in exclusive fullscreen stays on top.');
H(/^tip:which screen the scare pops up on/i, '🖱️ Which screen', 'Every screen at once (the default), or only the screen your mouse is on.');
H(/^tip:play the scare's sound on this pc too/i, '🔊 Sound', 'Plays the scare sound on this PC too. Off by default: the alerts already play it on stream and on your phone, and if OBS records your desktop sound viewers would hear it twice.');
H(/^tip:scare me for/i, '😱 Which alerts', 'Pick which alerts pop a scare up on your screen.');
H(/^tip:pop a (small|medium|big) scare/i, '😱 Try a scare', 'Pops that scare up right now (on every screen, or the screen your mouse is on if you picked that), so you can see how it looks over a game.');
H(/^tip:which scare (100 bits|1,000 bits|a \$30 tip|a 20 gift sub bomb|a raid of 5) gets/i, '😱 Which scare?', 'Shows which scare (small / medium / big) that alert would get. Nothing pops up.', ['test']);
H(/^🎟️ nobody waiting$/i, '🎟️ Nobody waiting', 'Nobody has a marathon battle in the line right now. When someone does, this button runs the first one.');
H(/^tip:show the total live time on stream/i, '⏱️ On stream', 'Shows the total live time on the marathon overlay in every marathon scene (in 🎮 gameplay next to the small counter at the top). Only time you are live counts.');
H(/^tip:start the marathon clock at 0:00:00 now/i, '🏁 Start counting now', 'The total live time starts at 0:00:00 now. From then on it adds up all your live time, even across stream restarts (it pauses while you are offline).');
H(/^tip:automatic: adds up this stream/i, '🔁 Automatic', 'Adds up this stream and the ones right before it when you were offline less than 6 hours in between, so restarting the stream for the co-stream counts as one marathon. A longer break starts it over.');
H(/^tip:show only how long this stream has been live/i, '📺 This stream only', 'Shows only how long the stream that is on right now has been live.');
H(/^tip:set the time by hand/i, '✏️ Fix the time', 'Type the total live time it should show (hours:minutes), like if the stream dropped or Movie Royal was closed. It keeps counting from there.');
H(/^tip:which corner the live time shows in/i, '⏱️ Corner', 'Which corner of the screen the total live time shows in. In 🎮 gameplay scenes it sits next to the small battles owed counter at the top instead.');
H(/^tip:show the total live time and the live times/i, '⏱️ Show the counter', 'Shows the total live time right now and the live times it adds up. Nothing changes.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:see the overlay with the live time/i, '👀 Preview', 'Opens the marathon overlay with a pretend live time, so you can see it.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:see the small gameplay counter with the live time/i, '🎮 Small one', 'Opens the small gameplay counter with the live time next to it (pretend).', ['test']);
H(/^tip:which stream new battles link to on the website/i, '▶ VOD links', 'Shows which Twitch stream new battles link to on the viewer website and whether the newest battles have a VOD link. After a stream restart new battles link to the new VOD; a VOD you delete stops getting links. Nothing changes.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:switch the mics by themselves when you change scenes/i, '🔁 Mic auto switch', 'When you change scenes in OBS: 🍳 Cooking = your wireless mics on and your PC mic (GoXLR) muted; any other marathon scene = the wireless mics off and your PC mic back on (only the mics it muted come back). Scenes from your normal OBS setup are left alone. Press to turn it on / off.');
H(/^tip:right now: your pc mic on/i, '🎙️ PC mic', 'Right now: your PC mic (GoXLR) back on and the wireless mics off, whatever scene you are on.');
H(/^tip:right now: the wireless mics on/i, '🍳 Cooking mics', 'Right now: the wireless mics on and your PC mic muted, whatever scene you are on.');
H(/^tip:pick which obs mics count as your pc mic/i, '⚙ Which mics', 'Pick which OBS mics get muted while you are cooking: every mic that is on (except the wireless ones), or only the ones you tick.');
H(/^tip:count “.*” as your pc mic/i, '🎙️ PC mic', 'Tick it to have it muted while you are in the Cooking scene (and turned back on after).');
H(/^tip:what (going to|leaving) the cooking scene would/i, '🎙️ Mic switch test', 'Asks OBS what switching would mute and turn on. Nothing changes.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:when someone whose battle has waited/i, '🔔 Chat reminders', 'When someone with a marathon battle that has been in the line 30+ minutes (you pick the minutes) types in chat, the bot says in chat “@you … is here and has a battle waiting”, so you can run it while they are here. Once per person every 30 minutes. Press to turn it on / off. Key: R on the Marathon tab.');
H(/^tip:how long a battle waits before you get reminded/i, '🔔 Minutes', 'How long a battle has to be in the line before the bot reminds you when that person chats.');
H(/^tip:show the reminder for the first person in the line/i, '🔔 Show the reminder', 'Shows what the bot would say in chat for the first person in the line. Nothing is sent.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:put a pretend \$5 tip battle in the line first/i, '💵 Add a pretend battle', 'Puts a pretend $5 tip battle (🧪) in the line so you can try the reminder.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:stop the text to speech that's talking right now/i, '⏭️ Skip voice', 'Stops the text to speech that is reading a tip / bits / channel point message right now (the StreamElements jump-scare alerts). It types the skip command (!skiptts) in your chat as you; every copy of the alerts hears it, on stream and on your phone. The next message still gets read. Key: K on the Marathon tab.');
H(/^tip:stop the text to speech and don't read any more/i, '🔇 Mute TTS', 'Stops the voice and stops reading messages until you press 🔊 Unmute TTS (it types !ttsoff in your chat as you). The alerts and their scares still play, they just stay quiet. Key: M on the Marathon tab.');
H(/^tip:let the text to speech read messages again/i, '🔊 Unmute TTS', 'Lets the text to speech read tip / bits / channel point messages again (types !ttson in your chat as you). Key: M on the Marathon tab.');
H(/^tip:change the chat commands the tts buttons type/i, '✏️ Commands…', 'The chat commands the TTS buttons type. Keep them the same as in your StreamElements alert settings (Text to speech → the skip command) or the alerts won\'t hear them.');
H(/^tip:show the commands the tts buttons type/i, '🔍 Show the commands', 'Shows what ⏭️ Skip voice / 🔇 Mute / 🔊 Unmute type in chat and whether Movie Royal can type in your chat. Nothing is sent.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:check that a 🍀 luck pick only goes on when you press/i, '🍀 Luck goes on at ▶ Run?', 'Checks that the 🍀 luck someone picks only goes on when you press ▶ Run for their battle (and comes back off if you cancel). Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:😴 after it wins it sits out the next battle/i, '😴 Sits out after a win', 'When this thing wins a marathon battle, it sits out the next battle (so it can\u2019t win twice in a row), then it\u2019s back in the one after. MERCY has it on. Practice battles don\u2019t count.');
H(/^tip:it won last time, so it sits out the next battle/i, '💤 Resting', 'It won the last battle, so it sits out the next one. Click to put it back in the next battle anyway.');
H(/^tip:check that a thing with 😴 sits out/i, '😴 Check it', 'Checks that a thing with 😴 (MERCY) is left out of the battle after it wins and is back in the one after. Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:set obs to 60 frames a second/i, '🎞️ Make it 60 fps', 'Sets OBS to 60 frames a second in the OBS profile you’re on (OBS → Settings → Video does the same). OBS only allows it while you’re not live or recording. 60 fps is twice the work for your graphics card.');
H(/^tip:set obs to 30 frames a second/i, '🎞️ 30 fps', 'Sets OBS back to 30 frames a second (half the work for your graphics card). Not while live or recording.');
H(/^tip:go back to the video before/i, '⏮ Video before', 'Goes back to the YouTube video before in that scene (☕ Be Right Back or 😴 Sleeping).');
H(/^tip:pause \/ play the/i, '⏯ Pause / play', 'Pauses or plays the YouTube video in that scene.');
H(/^tip:skip to the next video/i, '⏭ Next video', 'Skips to the next YouTube video in that scene. Key N skips in whichever one played last.');
H(/^tip:paste the youtube links/i, '✏️ Videos…', 'Paste YouTube links (videos or whole playlists) for the ☕ Be Right Back and 😴 Sleeping scenes, one per line, with 🔀 Shuffle for each. They loop forever, skip videos that can’t play outside YouTube, and pick up where they left off when the scene comes back.');
H(/^tip:how loud the youtube videos are/i, '🔊 Video volume', 'How loud the Be Right Back / Sleeping YouTube videos are. OBS’s Audio Mixer also has a slider for each.');
H(/^tip:the youtube links for the/i, '📺 Links', 'One YouTube link per line: a video (youtube.com/watch?v=… or youtu.be/…) or a playlist (a link with list=).');
H(/^tip:play the .* videos in a random order/i, '🔀 Shuffle', 'Plays that scene’s videos in a random order (playlists shuffle too).');
H(/^tip:check which of the pasted lines are youtube links/i, '🔍 Check links', 'Shows how many videos and playlists Movie Royal found in what you pasted, and which lines aren’t YouTube links. Nothing is saved.');
H(/^tip:save the youtube links/i, '💾 Save', 'Saves the links. A scene that’s playing starts the new list right away.');
H(/^tip:youtube links to try/i, '📺 Links to try', 'YouTube links to check or play, one per line. Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:check which of these lines are youtube/i, '🔍 Check links', 'Shows which lines are YouTube videos or playlists. Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:open the player with these links/i, '▶ Try the player', 'Opens the same YouTube player OBS uses, playing these links, in a window here. Nothing is saved.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:read every chat message out loud on your speaker/i, '🔈 Read chat to me', 'Turns reading chat out loud on or off. A Windows voice reads every chat message on the speaker you pick (your headphones), so only you hear it: it never goes on stream. It is a different voice from your alerts and it leaves cheers, channel point messages and highlighted messages out (the alerts read those). Commands (!…), known bots and your own messages are skipped; links are said as “a link”, emotes are left out. When chat gets busy, older messages are skipped so it keeps up. Key: V.');
H(/^tip:stop the chat message being read right now/i, '⏭️ Skip message', 'Stops the chat message the chat voice is reading right now and goes on to the next one. Key: B.');
H(/^tip:forget the chat messages waiting to be read/i, '🧹 Clear', 'Throws away the chat messages waiting to be read, so the chat voice catches up with chat.');
H(/^tip:hear what the chat voice sounds like/i, '🔊 Test', 'Reads a short test line with the chat voice on the speaker you picked, so you can check only you hear it (watch the OBS sound meters: they shouldn’t move).');
H(/^tip:which speaker chat is read on/i, '🎧 Speaker', 'The speaker the chat voice plays on. Pick your headphones or another speaker the stream can’t hear. Nothing is read until you pick one, and if that speaker is unplugged the message is skipped (it never plays on another speaker). With a GoXLR: pick one of its outputs and untick it from the Broadcast Mix in the GoXLR app’s Routing, or use headphones plugged into the PC.');
H(/^tip:which windows voice reads chat/i, '🗣️ Chat voice', 'Which Windows voice reads chat. Your alerts keep their own voice (Brian), so you can tell chat and tips apart by ear. More voices: Windows Settings → Time & language → Speech.');
H(/^tip:how fast chat is read/i, '🐇 Speed', 'How fast the chat voice talks. Faster keeps up better when chat is busy.');
H(/^tip:chat voice volume/i, '🔉 Chat voice volume', 'How loud the chat voice is (on top of your speaker’s own volume).');
H(/^tip:say who's talking before the message/i, '👤 Say who’s talking', 'Says the chatter’s name before their message (“Viewer One: hello”). Untick to hear only the message.');
H(/^tip:don't read your own messages/i, '🙊 Skip my messages', 'Your own chat messages aren’t read out.');
H(/^tip:don't read chat commands/i, '❗ Skip !commands', 'Messages that start with ! (or /) aren’t read, like !respin or !mymovies.');
H(/^tip:show what the chat voice would say for this message/i, '🔍 What would it say?', 'Shows the words the chat voice would read for the pretend message (or why it would skip it). Nothing is read.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:read this pretend message out loud/i, '🔈 Read it out loud', 'Reads the pretend message on your picked speaker now, like a real chat message.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:the same message as a cheer/i, '💎 As a cheer', 'Shows that a cheer with bits is left out of the chat voice (your alerts read cheers).', ['test']);
H(/^tip:the same message as a channel point message/i, '⭐ As channel points', 'Shows that a channel point message is left out of the chat voice (your alerts read those).', ['test']);
H(/^tip:a chat command: left out/i, '❗ A command', 'Shows that chat commands are left out of the chat voice.', ['test']);
H(/^tip:ban spam bots that try to sell something/i, '🛡️ Spam bot ban', 'When someone’s first message in your chat sells viewers, followers, promotion or art (emotes / overlays) with a way to buy it (a site, “dot com”, Telegram, Discord, “DM me”), Movie Royal deletes the message and bans them. Subs, VIPs, mods and you are never touched. Every ban is listed under it with ↩️ Unban, and in History → Everything.');
H(/^tip:what happens to a spam bot/i, '🔨 What happens', 'Ban them (they can’t come back), time them out for a day, or only delete the message.');
H(/^tip:only look at someone's first messages/i, '🆕 Only new chatters', 'Only checks people who have never chatted in your channel before (Twitch marks their first message). Regulars are never checked. Untick to check every message from people who aren’t subs, VIPs or mods.');
H(/^tip:read the scenes obs has open right now/i, '🔄 Read my scenes from OBS', 'Movie Royal asks OBS which scenes it has open and makes a 🎞️ Scenes page with a key for each one (it also does this when you press 🎛️ Add). Do it again for your other set of scenes (like the marathon setup) after switching OBS to it.');
H(/^tip:what a scene key does in obs/i, '🎞️ Scene key', 'Goes live right away = the scene switches on stream. Preview first = with OBS Studio Mode on, the scene goes to the preview and you press Transition yourself (like OBS’s own scene keys set to preview).');
H(/^tip:forget the scene keys for this set/i, '✕ Forget these scenes', 'Takes this set of scenes off the Stream Deck pages next time you press Add (OBS isn’t changed).');
H(/^tip:scene: /i, '🎞️ Scene key', 'Switches OBS to this scene when you press it on the Stream Deck.');
H(/^tip:check obs when movie royal opens and every 10 minutes/i, '🔄 Keep OBS up to date', 'On = when Movie Royal opens and every 10 minutes it checks the things it put in OBS for you (celebration, roll call, your videos, and in dev mode the marathon counter + scenes) and puts back anything missing. After an update it adds any new OBS pieces too. It never moves what you placed and never switches your scene.');
H(/^tip:check obs right now and add anything/i, '🔄 Check OBS now', 'Checks OBS right away and adds anything Movie Royal should have there. The list under it shows what it found.');
H(/^tip:on = in obs in the scenes you picked/i, '🎬 Video on / off', 'On = the video is in OBS in the scenes you picked. Off = taken out of OBS but kept on this list, so you can turn it back on.');
H(/^tip:pick which obs scenes this video goes in/i, '🎬 Scenes', 'Tick the OBS scenes this video plays in. It goes behind everything, fills the screen and loops. Scenes you untick lose it.');
H(/^tip:use a different video file for this one/i, '📂 File', 'Swap the video file this one plays. OBS starts playing the new file right away, in the same spot.');
H(/^tip:when the video goes into a scene, switch off/i, '🙈 Hide the scene\'s background', 'When the video is put into a scene, Movie Royal switches off that scene\'s own full-screen background (its title card, or an overlay named after the scene like “Starting Overlay”) so the video is what shows. Turn the video off and those come back. 🌴 Ready-made videos (like the Vice backgrounds in your Videos folder) have it on.');
H(/^tip:play it from the start in obs/i, '🔄 Restart', 'Plays the video from the start in OBS. Use it after you replaced the file on your PC with a new version (same name).');
H(/^tip:take it out of obs and off this list/i, '🗑 Remove video', 'Takes the video out of every OBS scene and off this list. The file stays on your PC.');
H(/^tip:videos in your videos folder/i, '➕ Pick a video', 'The videos in your Windows Videos folder, newest first. Pick one, then ➕ Add.');
H(/^tip:pick a video file anywhere on your pc/i, '📂 Browse', 'Opens a window to pick a video file from anywhere on your PC.');
H(/^tip:add this video, then pick its scenes/i, '➕ Add video', 'Adds the video, then asks which OBS scenes it goes in.');
H(/^tip:the video file's address on this pc/i, '📄 File address', 'Or paste the full address of a video file on this PC, then ➕ Add.');
H(/^tip:open settings → 🎥 obs → 🎬 my videos/i, '🎬 My videos', 'Opens Settings → 🎥 OBS → 🎬 My videos, where you add your own videos (backgrounds, starting / ending screens) and pick their OBS scenes.');
H(/^tip:check obs and add anything missing \(the same/i, '🔄 OBS test', 'Runs the 🔄 Keep OBS up to date check right now and shows what it found.');
H(/^tip:make the pages and hand them to the stream deck app/i, '🎛️ Add the pages to my Stream Deck', 'Makes the Movie Royal Stream Deck pages (with their pictures) and opens each one in the Stream Deck app, which asks if you want to import it. Every key presses a Movie Royal button in the background, so it works while you’re in a game. Press it again after an update adds new buttons.');
H(/^tip:which of your stream deck profiles the bottom-left home key/i, '🏠 Home key', 'The bottom-left key on every Movie Royal page. Pick which of your Stream Deck profiles it switches to (it finds one called “Home” by itself), or leave it empty and drag your own Home button there.');
H(/^tip:press any button from the test tab, like the stream deck/i, '🧪 Try a button', 'Opens the 🎛️ Stream Deck buttons card in the Test tab, where you can press any key the same way the Stream Deck does.');
H(/^tip:download just this page as a stream deck file/i, '⬇️ One page', 'Downloads that one page as a Stream Deck file. Double-click it to import it into the Stream Deck app.');
H(/^tip:make a new secret address/i, '🔑 New secret key', 'Each Stream Deck key goes to a secret address on this PC so web pages can’t press Movie Royal’s buttons. A new key makes a new address: the pages you already added stop working until you add them again.');
H(/^tip:which stream deck button to press/i, '🎛️ Which button', 'Pick a Stream Deck button to press from the Test tab.');
H(/^tip:press this button the way the stream deck would/i, '🎛️ Press it', 'Presses that Stream Deck button exactly like your Stream Deck does (same secret address). It really does the thing.');
